# Semgrep's built-in ignore list drops `tests/` wholesale. That silently made
# `semgrep scan --config p/python src tests` in .github/workflows/ci.yml scan
# `src` only, while the workflow named `tests` as a target: a gate whose stated
# scope was wider than its real one. Declaring the scope here makes the two
# agree. Defining this file replaces the built-in list entirely, so the
# exclusions that still matter are restated.
:include .gitignore

.git/
.venv/
dist/
build/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
